Chapter 02 - Treatment of Airway-Esophageal Fistulas
John Smith, Emily Doe
Abstract
Airway-esophageal fistulas require multidisciplinary management.
Keywords
fistula, stent, airway
Etiology
Benign and malignant causes contribute to fistula formation.
Diagnosis
Cross-sectional imaging and bronchoscopy are recommended.
Management
Covered stent placement and tissue sealants are typical therapies.
Follow-up
Patients require surveillance for restenosis and stent migration.
